The waiter looks at me and smiles.
"Good day, what would you like?" he asks.
I already know exactly what I want.
"Good day," I answer.
"I would like a large coffee, please."
He nods briefly.
"And could I please have a piece of chocolate cake?"
I point to the cake.
The waiter smiles again.
"Of course, very gladly," he says.
He types everything into the cash register.
"Just take a seat."
"I will bring the coffee and the cake to your table."
"Thank you very much," I say politely.
That is really good service.
I turn around and walk back to my seat.
